  "markdown": "Material family\n\n# Hand-painted scenic papers\n\nScenic and panelled papers, in the manner of houses such as de Gournay and Fromental. We hang them.\n\n![de Gournay hand-painted wallpaper with brass wall lights, a private residence, London.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/brand-de-gournay-01-800.webp)\n\nde Gournay hand-painted wallpaper installed in a private London residence, photographed under the room’s wall lights. The scene must be planned around these fixed fittings.Mr Wallcover project photograph, April 2018.[Our installation record](https://www.instagram.com/p/BhcaLpanOEf/)\n\nBefore you choose\n\n**Consider it when**\n: The scene should be designed around the room and its focal points.\n\n**The trade-off**\n: Doors, corners and furniture can interrupt the composition.\n\n**Before ordering**\n: Agree elevations, panel sequence, supplier proof and finished dimensions.\n\n01 · The finish\n\n## Joins\n\nPanels follow a sequence. The scene has to meet across doors, windows and corners. The set-out starts from a fixed point.\n\n02 · The setting\n\n## Where it belongs\n\nSuites and drawing rooms\n\n03 · Installation\n\n## Handling\n\nA sound wall, time, and the maker’s instruction on lining.\n\n04 · Living with it\n\n## Care\n\nAs the maker specifies. These are not washable contract surfaces.\n\nDigital colour is a guide. Order a cutting or a sample before you commit to a room. Some makers’ own sample routes are listed under [official buying routes](https://www.mrwallcover.com/buying-routes/). We can install material you have already bought, or source a family and install it. Either way, the next step is a short note about the room.\n\nBefore you order\n\n## For a high-value order\n\n- Workmanship is guaranteed for twelve months. [The aftercare page](https://www.mrwallcover.com/aftercare/) sets out what is covered.\n- Public liability, employers' liability and professional indemnity details are available on request.\n- Risk assessments and method statements (RAMS) on every job, with Dorin Burcus supervising on site.\n- A core team of six wallpaper hangers and six decorators who work together every day, scaling to 25–35 skilled tradespeople for large hotel programmes.\n- [For designers and architects](https://www.mrwallcover.com/professionals/designers/)\n- [Download the specification schedule (CSV)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/downloads/wallcovering-specification-schedule.csv)\n- [Trade and contractors](https://www.mrwallcover.com/trade/)\n\nIllustrative material study · confirm the actual finish with a sample\n\nPause motion\n\nSave to shortlist\n\nSaved on this device only.\n\n[Discuss this material](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=source&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Ahand-painted) [I already have it](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=install&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Ahand-painted)\n\n[How we install it](https://www.mrwallcover.com/services/hand-painted-wallpaper-installation/)\n\nInstallation experience\n\n## On the record\n\nAt [Brown's Hotel, Mayfair](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/) the scheme includes scenic and chinoiserie wallcoverings, among them Lewis & Wood's Adam's Eden. At a [tea house in West London](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/tea-house-jaillon-studio/) for Jaillon Studio, the garden room is a panoramic scenic paper of a swan lake and flowering hydrangeas. We have also installed de Gournay and Fromental papers, including a large volume of Fromental at Four Seasons Ten Trinity Square.\n\nThe [scenic set-out guide](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/hand-painted-murals-set-out/) covers elevations, panel sequence and finished dimensions, and [hand-painted wallpaper installation](https://www.mrwallcover.com/services/hand-painted-wallpaper-installation/) explains how we hang them.\n\nPlan the detail\n\n## Useful reading\n\n- [Hand-painted papers and murals](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/hand-painted-murals-set-out/)\n- [Designer checklist](https://www.mrwallcover.com/advice/designer-specification-checklist/)\n\nFrom our projects\n\n## Selected work\n\n- [Brown's Hotel, Mayfair](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/browns-hotel-mayfair/)\n- [A tea house in West London, for Jaillon Studio](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/tea-house-jaillon-studio/)\n- [Raffles London at The OWO, Whitehall](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/raffles-london-the-owo/)\n- [Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/)\n\nMakers installed\n\n## Hand-painted scenic papers: makers we have hung\n\nEach in our own photograph of its product on the wall. Naming a maker records an installation, not an endorsement.\n\n- ![de Gournay hand-painted wallpaper with brass wall lights, a private residence, London.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/brand-de-gournay-01-800.webp)\n\n### de Gournay\n\nInstalled at a private residence, London, 2018. [See the post](https://www.instagram.com/p/BhcaLpanOEf/).\n\n- ![Collage of Fromental silk wallcovering details in a hotel room, Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/fs-ig-01-800.webp)\n\n### Fromental\n\nInstalled at [Four Seasons Hotel London at Ten Trinity Square](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/four-seasons-ten-trinity-square/).\n\nHand-painted scenic papers: send a short note about the room, or tell us you already have the material.\n\n[Discuss this material](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=source&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Ahand-painted) [I already have it](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/?intent=install&service=wallcovering&topic=material%3Ahand-painted)\n\n[How we install hand-painted scenic papers](https://www.mrwallcover.com/services/hand-painted-wallpaper-installation/)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder\n",
